# TypeScript standards

- Use `strict` TypeScript settings (don’t relax without a clear reason).
- Prefer `zod` schemas at API boundaries (request parsing/validation).
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` + narrowing when needed.
- Prefer named exports (default export only for Next.js pages/layouts where idiomatic).
- Handle errors explicitly; never swallow exceptions silently.

